          ],
          "depiction": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/assets/img/workflows/named-query-execution.svg",
          "description": "Universal execution of audited named SPARQL queries against W3C RDF 1.1 N-Quads distributions across CLI, MCP, and Web runtimes. Governed by skill `named-query-execution` and schema `schemas/kg/nquads-distribution.ts`.\n\nCRITICAL INVARIANTS:\n1. FAIL-CLOSED GRAPH AVAILABILITY GUARD: Execution verifies all declared requiredSubgraphs are present in the Oxigraph store before SPARQL evaluation; missing partitions raise MissingPartitionError rather than returning silently incomplete results.\n2. SPARQL INJECTION PREVENTION: Parameters are strictly validated against manifest NamedQueryDef parameter schemas; IRIs and literals are escaped and substituted into pre-audited templates.\n3. UNIFIED THREE-SURFACE PARITY: Identical query semantics and result envelopes across CLI (bun run cat nquads:query), MCP (nquads-query tool), and Web (oxigraph-query-client.js).\n4. SCOPED GRAPH MATCHING: Triple patterns match inside GRAPH ?g { ... } or GRAPH <iri> { ... } to conform to W3C N-Quads 4th-slot named graph semantics.",
          "enforcement": "strict",
          "flowCount": 14,
          "inSubgraph": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/directory/kg-ops",
          "name": "Execute audited named queries over partitioned W3C N-Quads distributions",
          "nodeCount": 14,
